      title: 'A picnic for six friends', instruction: 'Nghe hai lượt. Chưa mở script. Ghi từ khóa rồi thuật lại.',
      lines: ['LẦN 1 · Ý CHÍNH', '1. What are the friends planning?', '2. When do they want to meet?', '3. How many people want to join?', 'LẦN 2 · CHI TIẾT', '1. How many people don’t eat meat?', 'What can Mai and Ben bring?', '2. What do both parks have?', 'Does either park have a café?', '3. Why does everyone have a bottle?', 'What does Lan need to send tonight?', 'Thuật lại 6–8 câu. Dùng ít nhất 5 cụm chỉ lượng và nêu điều cần chuẩn bị.'],
      dialogue: null,
      notes: 'Read twice in clear American English at about 105–120 words per minute. First gist, then detail. Keep the script hidden until the first retell. Answers: a picnic / Saturday / six; two / Mai fruit, Ben water; plenty of space / no; fewer bags and less rubbish / more information. SCRIPT: Hi, I’m Lan. Most of my friends work during the week, so six of us want to have a picnic on Saturday. Almost all of us like local food, but two of us don’t eat meat. We have a few dishes in mind, and each person can bring something. Mai has a little time on Friday, so she can buy some fruit. Ben has very little time, but he can bring water. We don’t need much equipment, just a few food boxes and enough cups for everyone. There are two parks near the river. Both of them have plenty of space, but neither of them has a café. Either park is fine if we bring our own drinks. We want fewer bags and less rubbish, so everyone has a reusable bottle. Our plan isn’t perfect yet. Some of my friends have questions, so I need to send them more information tonight.',
